<title>KAZAKHSTAN: SocGen to open subsidiary in Kazakhstan.</title>
<headline>SocGen to open subsidiary in Kazakhstan.</headline>
<dateline>ALMATY 1997-07-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>French bank Societe Generale has received a licence from the Kazakhstan National Bank to open a subsidiary in Almaty, a deputy bank chairman told reporters on Wednesday.</p>
<p>&quot;This will be a bank with foreign capital...In Kazakhstan it will have the status of a resident,&quot; said Anvar Saydenov.</p>
<p>He said the new bank -- Societe Generale Kazakhstan -- will have capital of $6 million.</p>
<p>As of July 1 this year, 96 banks were operating in the former Soviet republic, including nine banks with foreign capital.</p>
<p>--Murat Buldekbayev, Almaty Newsroom, +7 3272 509410</p>
